    "lineas":  [
                   {
                       "texto":  "Part three. Years have passed. You are twenty-one now.",
                       "pausa":  0.8
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "Becoming a knight costs a fortune: horses, armour, a sword, and servants of your own.",
                       "pausa":  0.8
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "So much that many squires never became knights at all. Some kings had to order rich men to do it.",
                       "pausa":  0.8
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "But your lord will pay. The night before, by tradition, you pray in the chapel until dawn.",
                       "pausa":  0.8
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "In the morning, the great hall is full. Everyone is watching.",
                       "pausa":  0.8
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "You kneel. Your lord touches your shoulder with his sword. This is the dubbing.",
                       "pausa":  1.0
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "Then you are given spurs, the mark of a knight.",
                       "pausa":  0.8
                   },
                   {
                       "texto":  "Tonight, a new boy sleeps on your old straw mattress. Would you have stayed a squire?",
                       "pausa":  0.3
                   }
               ],
